  "assertions": [
    "PairingResponse is the sole larger pre-auth response: its total framed size must be <= 320 B (spec §4.2, §10 TM-6 as revised 2026-11-12); this vector's is smaller and the size bound is asserted.",
    "PairingResponse echoes the offered capabilities set unchanged (empty in v2.0; an empty repeated field is not encoded), plus server_random, the raw 32-byte Ed25519 identity key, binding (48 B), client_id (first 8 of SHA-256(client_public_key)) and the accepted display name.",
    "binding and binding_echo are TLS-Exporter outputs — fixture-fixed stand-ins (test-keys.json); the Client MUST verify binding equals its own derivation before sending PairingConfirm (pairing.md §6.3).",
    "client_proof = ECDSA-P256-SHA256(identity key, TLV(1,'audio-share v2 pairing confirm') || TLV(2,binding)), 64-byte r||s, exactly one hash (pairing.md §6.3.1); the Server verifies it BEFORE persisting or answering PairingResult(OK).",
    "PairingResult(OK) has an empty Status (present, no fields) — pairing persisted; state moves to NEGOTIATING and the Client next sends Negotiate (spec §5.3).",
    "binding_context and the derived SAS code are recorded below as hand-derivation checks; binding/sas_seed themselves are fixture-fixed exporter stand-ins."
  ],
  "size_bounds": [
    {
      "frame": "pairing_response",
      "max_frame_bytes": 320,
      "rule": "spec §4.2/§10 TM-6: successful PairingResponse <= 320 B Frame.length"
    }
  ],
